WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.580
<b>A quick primer!</b>

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.580
<b>RECAPPING THE STORY THUS FAR</b>

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:04.170
A quick primer. Recapping the story thus far.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.040
Shamiko... Thou must awaken, Shamiko...

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.210
Open your eyes.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.130
Who are you?

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.170
Ah! What happened to me?

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.880
My memories are... really fuzzy.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.460
Am I in a hospital room? Or are these ruins?

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.380
H-hello, is there anybody out here?

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.920
That looks like Anri, one of my classmates
from Sakuragaoka High School.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.710
And Ogura? What's wrong with you two?!

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:35.960
We turn zombie... we zombies now...

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.460
We like bite... we biting zombies...

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.170
Oh, I see!

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.880
S-somebody help!
We bite you!<b>
</b>We zombies!<b></b>

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.790
Are you awake, my adorable descendant?
Guess who's here!

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.670
<b>GUESS WHO'S HERE!!</b>

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.580
A-Ancestor?!

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.830
What is going on?

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.750
No time to explain! We gotta move!

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.250
Uh, you've got shards of glass stuck in you!

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.000
Totally worth it for my window-smashing entrance!

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:59.580
So, it turns out you got hit by that dump truck
back in episode 1 of season 1

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.790
and have been in some kinda cold sleep ever since!

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:02.960
Huh, what "episode"?

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.210
In the meantime, this M-virus sorta thingy
spread throughout the world

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.880
and turned a buncha stuff into zombies,

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.290
so now Tama City is kinda like one of those
post-apocalyptic hellscapes!

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.750
Could you be any more vague?

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.330
Don't think, just feel!

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:17.750
All of the survivors have taken refuge
at Shopping Center Maruma and formed a government.
Zombie... zombie...<b></b>

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.460
We'll have to take a merry little stroll
to get there. Let's move!

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.460
O-okay!

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.710
No way, we can't accept any newcomers.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:30.580
<b>Soverign State of Tama City</b>

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:30.580
<b>Leader: Momo Chiyoda</b>

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.250
We're already struggling with our limited food supplies,

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.880
and this girl obviously can't fight,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.580
which means she's just baggage that will drag us down.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.710
This is my cute little descendant
we're talking about! You gotta take her in!

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:34.420
Traooosh...

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.460
Making special exceptions is asking for trouble.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.750
What the heck?! Are you hungry enough
to go dumpster diving for food?!

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.880
Um, that's not it! I just noticed this stuff is still edible!

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.250
You shouldn't let vegetable rinds like these go to waste.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.290
You can slice them up
and use them in tempura or stir-fry.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.040
Also, you've peeled off way too much.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.250
Furthermore, radishes and such
can sprout and be eaten again.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.290
Just dip the calyx in water
and leave them on the windowsill.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.540
She's amazing...

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.960
As for pumpkin seeds, you should dry them out and...

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.880
We get it! Fine, we'll accept you as one of our citizens!

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:02.170
Hooray, this means we don't have to eat
any more of Momo's glowing food!

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.040
<b>HUG</b>

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.880
Praise be Shamiko!

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:08.630
Praise be Shamiko! Long live Shamiko! Long live Shamiko!

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:08.630
And so, my life surviving the zombie apocalypse began...

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:15.330
<b>THE HUMANS ARGUE AMONGST THEMSELVES</b>

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:15.330
<b>WHILE IGNORING THE ZOMBIES!!</b>

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.540
THE HUMANS ARGUE AMONGST THEMSELVES
WHILE IGNORING THE ZOMBIES!

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.330
I'm sick and tired of not being the leader!

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:20.290
We like bite... we biting zombies...

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.580
Therefore, Shamiko and I
hereby declare our independence!

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.920
Huh?! I'm going, too?!

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.290
No, leave Shamiko with us.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:26.540
<b>THEN A POST-APOCALYPTIC DJ</b>

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:26.540
<b>COMES FROM OUT OF NOWHERE!</b>

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.080
THEN A POST-APOCALYPTIC DJ
COMES FROM OUT OF NOWHERE!

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.040
It's Friday night, which means it's time for...
Enjoyable End Times on Tama Sakura Radio.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.250
Today's request comes from a listener by the name of...

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.000
"One should never put new deer antler to the nose and sniff it."

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.000
Oh my gosh... other survivors!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.460
<b>THE BARRICADE!</b>

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.460
<b>THE GIRL WITH A BLEEDING-HEART FOR DOGS</b>

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.460
<b>CARELESSLY OPENS</b>

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.000
THE GIRL WITH A BLEEDING-HEART FOR DOGS
CARELESSLY OPENS THE BARRICADE!

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.830
Good boy, come this way.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.880
<b>THE BELOVED MENTOR</b>

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.880
<b>ENDS UP BECOMING A ZOMBIE!</b>

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.290
THE BELOVED MENTOR
ENDS UP BECOMING A ZOMBIE!

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.040
Oopsie-doopsie!

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.040
<b>Oopsie-doopsie!</b>

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.750
ANCESTOOOOOOR!

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:58.920
Shamiko... you... have to shoot me...

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.420
This is just awful!

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.500
It's all lies! This recap is nothing but lies!

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.880
Yeah, but it was super thrilling, right?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.580
It wasn't thrilling at all, it was heartbreaking!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.170
Oh...

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:13.130
I mean, it got so bad that you were turned into a zombie!
And it looked like I was about to shoot you!

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.500
Well, any episode where the mentor dies
and their student surpasses them

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.750
is guaranteed to be a masterpiece.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.630
I hope we can do that around season 4 episode 9 or so!

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.210
There aren't going to be any "seasons"!

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:22.580
But get this, rumor is that the actress for Lilith
had to resign from her role

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.000
after making a fuss about her paycheck.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.790
Quit making up backstories that nobody needs!

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.290
Aw, but I worked so hard on them...

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.880
Anyways, we have a big problem. That recap
was so packed full of content that we're outta time now.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:32.330
What?

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.000
You're going to wake up from this dream.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.710
Good luck, Shamiko.
I'm counting on you to explain the rest...

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:38.920
...the rest...

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.170
...the rest...

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:40.830
...the rest...

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.250
WHAAAAAAAT?!

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.540
A fake recap...

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.960
Oh! It was just a dream!

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:53.170
Shamiko, the segment's about to come to a close!
Hurry up and give everyone the real recap!

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:53.880
What "segment"?!

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:54.670
Okay! Go!

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.460
Well... um, um, um, um, um...

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:58.920
I'm a demon girl!

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.750
<b>DEMON</b>

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.580
And my dad is inside of a mikan box!

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:07.170
My arch-enemy came to the dark side
after things got out of whack,

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.290
it was a real surprise until she reverted back.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.080
<b>TO THE DARK SIDE</b>

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.630
She sucks at explaining, huh?

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.960
This is the tale of a young demon girl
who received her powers overnight,

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:22.750
and now works with the neighborhood magical girls
to protect the city, while also cooking and stuff.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.790
Or something to that effect!

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.920
Doki doki wa kore kara!

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:48.710
Kiseki okoru yokan

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:55.960
Henachoko sajikagen de ii desho iza susume!

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:58.920
Ichika bachika yukeru donna basho datte

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:03.630
Motto kikasete core no oto made

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:08.420
Futari te o awasetara kowaku nai yo

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.920
Komatta toki ni wa

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.210
Omoidashite

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:16.960
Kimi ga iru tte koto

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:24.580
Onaji sora futari de miagete

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:28.960
Waraiatte tsurai koto mo norikoechaou

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:34.210
Dareka no tame ni ganbaru koto

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:41.380
Sore mo warukunai kyou mo tonari de

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:48.460
Tokimeki wa kore kara!

00:05:56.170 --> 00:06:01.040
<b>A SHORT BREAK!!</b>

00:05:56.170 --> 00:06:01.040
<b>THE DEMONIC SUMMER FESTIVAL</b>

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.380
Summer vacation picture diary: July Xth. Sunny.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:10.040
<b>AFTER DIGGING INTO THE DIRT</b>

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:10.040
<b>OF SOME FACTORY RUINS,</b>

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:10.040
<b>I FOUND A WEAPON</b>

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:10.040
<b>THAT BELONGS TO MY FATHER</b>

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:10.040
<b>WHO IS CURRENTLY SEALED AWAY.</b>

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:10.040
<b>JULY XTH</b>

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:10.040
<b>SUNNY</b>

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.500
After digging into the dirt of some factory ruins,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:10.040
I found a weapon that belongs to my father
who is currently sealed away.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:18.380
<b>I ATE SOME SORT OF FOOD AT</b>

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:18.380
<b>MY PART-TIME JOB THAT MAKES</b>

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:18.380
<b>PEOPLE FORGET THINGS. AND SO</b>

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:18.380
<b>I DON'T REMEMBER ANY OF THIS.</b>

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:18.380
<b>FOR A FEW DAYS</b>

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:18.380
<b>STARTING ON</b>

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:18.380
<b>AUGUST XST</b>

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:18.380
<b>WEATHER UNKNOWN</b>

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.710
For a few days starting on August Xst. Weather unknown.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.880
I ate some sort of food at my part-time job that makes
people forget things.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:18.330
And so I don't remember any of this.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.170
I got lost while searching around in my own memories

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:28.080
<b>I GOT LOST WHILE SEARCHING AROUND</b>

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:28.080
<b>IN MY OWN MEMORIES AND MY</b>

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:28.080
<b>ARCH-ENEMY CAME OVER TO</b>

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:28.080
<b>THE DARK SIDE TO SAVE ME.</b>

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:28.080
<b>AUGUST XTH</b>

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:28.080
<b>DARK</b>

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:25.920
and my arch-enemy came over
to the dark side to save me.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.080
Whoa, you really put a lot of work
into this drawing of Momochiyo!

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.540
I gotta say, this summer vacation diary
of yours is straight fire!

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.290
I really wonder how it ended up like this...

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:35.540
Today is a school day.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.250
Things have been a mess lately,

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.880
but I'm gonna start acting like a proper ruler of darkness
by recruiting some followers!

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.040
I hope you'll be willing to lend me your support, Anri!

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:47.040
I'd be more than happy to, but... be real, Shamiko.
Was your vacation actually a vacation?

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:47.580
Huh?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.880
Well, thanks to your help, my summer vacation
was bigger and more sensational than ever!

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.040
Having a sensational vacation
doesn't make it a good one!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:52.670
<b>Flinch</b>

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:55.580
I mean, the last half of your diary was filled
with nothing but disasters!

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:59.670
Normal high schoolers don't inherit a weapon
from their dad during summer vacation, you know.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.330
P-point taken...

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.630
You need to scale it back a little bit.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:08.880
From what I see in your diary,
you were laid up in bed at least twice.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:13.880
And I noticed that you lost your memory at the café
I told you about... now I feel bad about it.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.210
What about if you just took it easy for a day?

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:16.960
Also...

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:17.380
Okay!

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:19.880
I haven't seen anybody
use this brand of journal in forever!

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.960
<b>SQUIDSKINE NOTEBOOK</b>

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.920
That reminds me, where is Momochiyo today?

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:26.460
Momo is with Mikan... oh, I mean, she's having
a strategy meeting with another magical girl right now.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:30.460
All right, then I'll get a hold of them for you.
So go and do whatever you want this afternoon!

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:33.250
Spend your summer vacation
like you're supposed to, by having some fun!

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:36.420
But I don't know what people do for fun
on summer vacation.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:38.830
Besides, you have to remember that I'm a demon...

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:42.960
That doesn't make a difference! The fact remains that
summer at the age of 15 only comes once in a lifetime!

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.330
Enjoy summer vacation!

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.500
<b>ALL ITEMS HERE</b>

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.500
<b>100 YEN</b>

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:51.670
You gotta spend at least one day taking it easy,
because that's how people recharge their batteries!

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:54.750
I wasn't expecting to suddenly have the day off.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:56.580
Momo!

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:57.380
Huh?

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.170
Momo and Mikan went out somewhere
after they finished their meeting.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:04.250
They were hauling huge dumbbells and
exercise bands with them in spite of the heat outside.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.630
Something about doing training to restore
Momo's magical power. I couldn't believe it.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.380
Aw, phooey...

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.670
Wait, did you want to go with them or something?!

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:15.500
Huh?! N-no way! I'm actually relieved
they didn't rope me into it!

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:21.250
This just doesn't feel right somehow...

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:26.170
Ancestor, what do you think a normal
summer vacation is supposed to be like?

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:29.790
That's a good question. We didn't have
any summer vacation back in Mesopotamia.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.290
All we had were dry season and rainy season.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:34.040
The dry season was so scorching hot
that it could kill people,

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:37.210
so it felt absolutely amazing to get
totally nude and take naps in the shade!

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:38.790
<b>MESOPOTAMIA</b>

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:38.790
<b>A LAWLESS LAND</b>

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:38.790
Nope. Next idea, please.

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.790
Well, we also enjoyed drinking wine
while naked in the shade...

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.290
That's even more out of the question!

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.290
Aw...

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.040
I guess I'll just go for a walk outside.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.710
<b>ASURA</b>

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.540
Good afternoon.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:52.040
Oh, what a pleasant surprise. It's good to see you, hun!

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.290
I heard about what happened with Sakura.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.670
I'm sure it's a tough job, but break a leg!

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.250
This is from the boss. It's on the house.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.380
Listen, Lico. I'm going to need you
to stop giving out free food in my name!

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:03.790
But it's okay this time.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:07.250
I've got a question for you two.
What do you think a normal summer vacation is like?

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.500
The first thing to come to mind for me is...

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.790
the beautiful sweat that students shed
after a summer of manual labor.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.750
We've got box lunches for sale! Buy tasty box lunches here!

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:17.170
<b>BOX LUNCHES 350 YEN</b>

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:17.170
<b>BOX LUNCHES 350 YEN</b>

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:15.750
This is what a normal summer vacation is like!

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:17.170
<b>This is what a</b>

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:17.170
<b>normal  summer</b>

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:17.170
<b>vacation is like!!</b>

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:16.920
That can't be right.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.170
<b>That can't</b>

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.170
<b>be right.</b>

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:19.540
No way! This doesn't feel right to me at all!

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.710
You go with the flow better than a fish, hun.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:26.040
I'm impressed that you kept it up as long as you did.
But, thank you, it was a huge help.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.630
Here is your compensation for today.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.920
Oh... thank you very much!

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:37.750
<b>COOL OFF</b>

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:37.750
<b>AT THE TAMA SAKURA</b>

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:37.750
<b>SHOPPING DISTRICT</b>

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:36.420
Our shopping district is having a "Beat the Heat Festival"
today. So we decided to sell special box lunches.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.460
A festival?

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.250
The food and beverage industry
essentially goes to war around this time of year.

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:43.670
It makes the concept of a "vacation" feel alien enough
to be from an ultra-distant galaxy.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:45.460
Sorry that I couldn't be of more help.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.580
It's okay. I'm sorry for bothering you.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:50.460
Hold your horses! No good summer vacation
goes without a festival!

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.210
You need to go out there and whoop it up, hun.

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:54.250
Come over here and let me dress you up in a yukata.

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:55.670
Huh? Do you really mean it?

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.290
Lookin' spiffy!

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.290
Th-thank you so much.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:03.000
Now I feel like I'm as rich as one of those oil barons!

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.670
I'm gonna go have the time of my life!

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.460
That's the spirit! You should find one of those
string-pulling prize stalls

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.380
and do it over and over until you win something!

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:12.790
Lico! Enough with your horrible advice! I heavily
recommend you avoid those string lotteries, Shamiko!

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.880
All right! Time to party hardy!

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.960
<b>Tama Sakura</b>

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.960
<b>Shopping District</b>

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:19.920
<b>YAKISOBA</b>

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.540
Weird, this isn't what I expected. Something feels off.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:35.540
My tail is as limp as a noodle. But why?

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:37.170
I went fishing for a yo-yo balloon!

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:42.960
<b>Plastic</b>

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:42.960
<b>Whacky-smacky katana!</b>

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:40.460
I got a plastic whacky-smacky katana!

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.540
I got some hot and crispy takoyaki
garnished with a frankfurter from Maruma's Meats!

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:48.710
That's too long! So hot!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:49.710
Plus a candy apple!

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.290
Wow! Candy apple!

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.250
And!

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.380
<b>Aaaaaand!</b>

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.540
Yukata!

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.170
Ponytail!

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:04.290
I've equipped myself with all the summer party goods
I can think of, but I still feel empty somehow. Why is that?

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:06.920
Do members of the Dark Clan
just have bad chemistry with summer?

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:10.210
This sucks. The vibe is all wrong when I'm alone.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:14.080
I just don't get it. I never used to feel this way before.

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:21.380
I guess I'll head back home.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.420
Attention guests, please be on the lookout
for a missing child.

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:28.540
The 15-year-old Shadow Mistress Yuko from Tama City.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:31.710
She's a short girl with naturally curly horns on her head.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.580
What the heck was that announcement?!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:35.540
Two of her minions are trying to find her.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.290
Please visit the service desk right away
if you have any information that may help.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.290
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:42.750
That's okay! It's no problem!

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:43.790
Huff! Puff!

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:47.290
Where's the joker who requested
they make such an unflattering announcement?!

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:50.880
<b>SERVICE DESK</b>

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:48.960
Oh, Shamiko. There you are.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.880
I figured it was you, Magical Girl!

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:52.790
I'm not some lost little girl, dang it!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:55.500
And consider the word "short" banned
from your vocabulary from this point forward!

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.580
But I will admit the "minions" part
was a nice confidence booster!

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.750
Huh? What's with the yukata?

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:03.380
Oh... they made me wear it
after I went to the café looking for you.

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:05.500
And there's some weird spell
preventing me from taking it off.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:09.380
It's my "Loose Clothes Suppression" spell!
You can take it off once the clock hits midnight.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.130
W-well, that's interesting...

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.210
We heard that you wanted some time
to take it easy, but...

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:21.790
you hadn't come home and it's so hot out
that we started to get a little worried.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:25.420
O-oh, I see. Well, now that you're here...

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.080
<b>Hee</b>

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.080
<b>Hee</b>

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:23.330
<b>Hee</b>

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:23.330
<b>Hee</b>

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.460
<b>Hee</b>

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.460
<b>Hee</b>

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:25.210
<b>Hee</b>

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:25.210
<b>Hee</b>

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.500
We're sorry for bothering you.

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:30.290
Let's get out of here, Mikan. This outfit is mortifying.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:31.540
Huh? No, wait!

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:33.250
What is it, Shamiko?

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:37.630
<b>Griiiip...</b>

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:37.130
You're just gonna turn tail and run from summer?!
I thought light was your main attribute!

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.500
What do you mean "run away" from summer?

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.580
Citrusly?

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:44.290
Whatever! You're not going anywhere
until you've absorbed some of the summer vibes!

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:46.830
Let's go! Come on, this way!

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.330
<b>GOLDFISH SCOOPING</b>

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.330
Whee! Whee!

00:12:56.420 --> 00:13:00.670
Whee! Whee! Whee!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.630
This is it. Now it's really hitting home.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:00.670
What's up?

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.790
I figured out that it's impossible
for a small-time demon girl like myself

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:05.420
to exhaust everything that summer has to offer alone.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.790
The energy of summer
is something that has to be divided.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:10.790
So the best way for a demon to spend their summer
is by sharing it with their minions!

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:15.250
<b>Take this!</b>

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:15.250
<b>Demonic</b>

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:15.250
<b>Takoyaki!</b>

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:12.670
Take this! Demonic takoyaki!

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.630
I really don't understand why
she's having such a hard time with summer...

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:16.290
Sneak.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:18.330
<b>FRANKFURTERS</b>

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:21.500
Let's come again next year!

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:22.290
Yes.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:24.500
Attention guests, this is a paging announcement.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:28.420
Ms. Fresh Peach, the malicious magical girl
from Tama City, you're wanted at the service desk.

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:33.040
The roughly 5,000-year-old, adorable singing
and dancing doll name Lilith is asking for you.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:37.790
That lottery has to be rigged! I couldn't win no matter
string what I pulled! Get your butt over here, Momo!
Harumph! Harumph! Harumph!<b></b>

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.710
Please hurry to the service desk and bring your wallet.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:43.040
What was that all about?

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.790
Did my ancestor come with you guys?

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:49.670
She kept seeing stuff that she wanted,
so we gave her some cash and left her behind.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:54.920
Ms. Fresh Peach from Tama City,
please hurry to the service desk with your wallet.

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:57.250
But I don't know this person she's trying to find.

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.500
Isn't "Fresh Peach" supposed to be you?

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.420
Nope. Nobody that I know!

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:04.330
<b>Smile</b>

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:02.170
Smile.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.250
Don't just feign pleasant ignorance and leave!

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:08.500
It's fine, because her soul will come back on its own
once her vessel runs out of power.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.540
We should still go and pick her up!

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:15.000
Don't give up, Shamiko! Create a good balance in
your life by making the time to goof around and have fun!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.790
<b>CAFÉ</b>

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.790
<b>ASURA</b>

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:18.790
<b>SOME TIME</b>

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:18.790
<b>LATER</b>

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:18.500
A few days have gone by since the festival ended.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.330
Thanks, Lico. I really appreciate you
lending me this yukata.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.670
Aw shucks, you didn't need to bring it back.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.670
It's nothing but a simple leaf.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:26.330
Huh?

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:27.210
Ta-da!

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:30.380
See? It's magic.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:32.920
One of many tricks we Huli jing can do!

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:38.920
Oh God... I paraded myself through
that whole festival while wearing nothing but a leaf.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:39.830
Shiver...

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.790
<b>MATH</b>

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:55.580
Are you hungry or something?

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.460
Certainly not!

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:59.210
I'm sitting here and struggling with
my summer homework as you can clearly see!

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:01.380
So much has been going on
that I'm not even close to finished!

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:05.080
I didn't take you for the type of demon
to actually get her homework done. Kudos.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.290
I haven't touched my homework at all.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.080
Well, I'm one of the most
noble demons out there! Wait, what?

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.080
You can't be serious! Students have to study!
That goes without saying!

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.830
Why would you avoid doing homework, Momo?

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:16.830
You're so smart!

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:18.500
I mean, let's be real here...

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:22.540
who doesn't leave the end of semester handout
with all the homework on it in their desk?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:25.250
I hope you're not expecting me to answer that!
Because I can't relate!

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.630
Right now I'm just feeling "meh, whatever" about it.

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:29.630
<b>MEH... WHATEVER...</b>

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.080
And that's definitely not a good thing!

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.920
A magical girl like you needs to be doing
the right thing and turning in her homework!

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:36.210
I am a magical girl, but I think I get a pass on this
since I went over to the dark side once.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:38.130
No, you don't! Don't try to spin it that way!

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.420
Just relax. I'll be sure to get it done little by little.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:42.330
By how little, exactly?!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.920
Y'know, step by step...

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.040
Look me in the eyes when you speak, please!

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:51.750
Now that I think about it, I've seen Momo just stuff her
test papers into her desk without a care in the world.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.210
Squashed into a total mess...

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.130
She's my tentative vassal who I share a bond with!

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.040
So I have to do what I can to support her!

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.290
No more letting your worksheets
get squashed into a total mess.

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:00.630
Let's get our homework done!

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:03.420
We'll do every activity and review all the material,

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.830
so that way we're in good shape
for the post-vacation test!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:10.000
Okay, sure, but you're gonna struggle on that test
no matter how much homework you do, right?

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:13.250
I see your skills as my arch-enemy are sharper than ever!

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:16.580
The real question is, why do they call it a "summer
vacation" but then saddle us with a bunch of homework?

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.460
Huh? Because studying through school is how we learn...

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:23.500
<b>CLOSE</b>

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:23.500
<b>ATTENTION</b>

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:23.330
Sure, but I pay close attention to what's taught in class
so that I can memorize everything during that time.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:29.040
Forcing us to meet a homework quota during our time off
sounds a awful lot like unpaid study time,

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:30.420
and that's illegal, right?

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.540
What's "unpaid study time"?

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:35.670
I think you should lift weights
and go jogging until you're strong enough

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:38.210
to protect this city from the school's evil scams!

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:40.790
M-maybe, I guess...? I'm not sure that's right...

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:42.580
I'm gonna use this precious summer vacation

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:45.040
to pour all of my stats into brute strength
so that I can protect you.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:51.750
<b>MATH</b>

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.330
Okay, let's ditch the books and get running!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:48.710
R-right!

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:51.750
Get your head on straight, Shamiko!
Don't let her fool you with all of that nonsense!

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:55.580
Why are you so interested
in making me do my homework, anyway?

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:59.130
B-because I have to fulfill my promise
with Ms. Sakura and watch after you!

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:02.290
Plus, I'm currently renting Ms. Sakura's core from her.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:05.880
By the way, it's totally cool if you wanna start
thinking of ME as your big sister!

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:07.580
We're on our way to being family, anyway!

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:08.380
Big sister?

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.630
<b>Smirk!</b>

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:13.380
You're lacking in the size department.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.210
Watch your mouth, missy!
You wanna take this outside?! I'll throw down with you!
Outrage! Outrage! Outrage!<b></b>

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:17.830
<b>Outrage!</b>

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:18.540
I'll make sure you never forget who your arch-nemesis is!
Outrage! Outrage! Outrage!<b></b>

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.420
For your information, my sister was also the type
to get her homework done at the very last minute.

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:22.080
What?!

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:24.330
Oh. Yeah, I can kinda imagine that.

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:26.920
So, like, apparently I was an orphan.

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:27.670
Huh?

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:32.210
I was too young to remember much of it,
but I guess I showed a lot of potential as a magical girl

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:34.380
and that's why my sister took me in.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.670
I had a problem with being anxious
around strangers back then,

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:41.210
and my sister was kind enough
to accompany me around to various places.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:45.710
But that caused her work to pile up until she rushed
to get it all done the day before it was due.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:47.040
The time... The time... The time hath...

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.210
Sounds like she was pretty foolhardy...

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:51.000
Listen, Momo. Due dates can always be extended
just like a rubber band!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.580
Now if you'll excuse me,
I need to go apologize to my teacher.

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:54.460
That's cool.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.210
So, yeah.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:57.380
That's definitely not a lesson you should take to heart!

00:17:58.420 --> 00:17:59.080
Come on!

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:00.670
Sit down!

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:03.040
Homework is like a promise we make to our teachers!

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.420
And there's nothing more important
than keeping promises!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:08.580
I'm going to keep watch
while you get your homework done today!

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:09.500
Meeeeh...

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.920
Get ready to pull an all-nighter!
Huff! Puff! Huff! Puff!<b></b>

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:09.960
<b>Huff!</b>

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:10.670
<b>Puff!</b>

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:11.500
<b>Huff!</b>

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:14.380
I'm gonna make you suffer just as much as I did
when you strapped me to that giant tire!
Huff! Puff! Huff! Puff!<b></b>

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:12.170
<b>Puff!</b>

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:12.960
<b>Huff!</b>

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:13.710
<b>Puff!</b>

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:14.460
<b>Huff!</b>

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:16.420
What kind of riceballs do you want for dinner?

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:19.920
I personally recommend the ones filled
with soy-glazed bonito flakes and little tempura bits!

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.130
Oh, Shamiko. It's painfully obvious
you want to have a sleepover.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.630
Your tail totally gives away how excited you are.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.630
First up, the essay! "My Dreams for the Future"!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.960
Man, writing essays is a total drag.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.540
Don't you just hate having to tell your teacher
about how you feel and stuff?

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.250
What kind of things do you wanna do in the future?

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.580
<b>MY DREAMS</b>

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.580
<b>FOR THE FUTURE</b>

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.580
<b>NOTHING IN</b>

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.580
<b>PARTICULAR.</b>

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:37.790
Nothing in particular.

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:38.580
Don't be ridiculous!

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:48.960
<b>CLENCH</b>

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:48.960
<b>CLENCH</b>

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:48.960
<b>CLENCH</b>

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:48.960
<b>CLENCH</b>

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:41.880
Okay. Pick up that pencil.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:45.670
Then write down "becoming a magical girl
who has been fully engulfed by the darkness."

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.920
Oh hey, I didn't know you were left-handed.

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.000
I refuse.

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:50.080
But why?!

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:53.210
Because it's gonna put undue pressure on me
after I grow up and look back on it!

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:54.380
Grumble, grumble, grumble.

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.540
Slink, slink, slink.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:58.250
Fine, let's shelve the essay. Next up: your diary!

00:18:57.170 --> 00:19:00.420
<b>SQUIDSKINE NOTEBOOK</b>

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.420
Oh come on, that one's not even mandatory.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:03.750
Well, I did mine. Just write about the days
that you found memorable!

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:03.750
<b>SQUIDSKINE NOTEBOOK</b>

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:10.290
<b>Hype</b>

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:10.290
<b>Hype</b>

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:10.290
<b>Hype</b>

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:10.290
<b>Hype</b>

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.920
Go on! Write about what happened on August Xth!

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:10.290
Hype, hype! Hype, hype!

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:10.290
I woke up, ate some food,
exercised, and then went to bed.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.250
Whaaaaat?! Don't lie to me!

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.380
You went to the dark side that day!
You came to save me!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.880
August Xth is the day that we celebrate
your descent into darkness!

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.750
You're being a real pain in the neck today, Shamiko!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:21.500
Go outside if you're gonna get noisy!

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:23.290
Sorry, Ma'am.
Sorry, Mom.<b></b>

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.130
<b>YOSHIDA</b>

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:29.500
I could write an essay if the subject
was about how cute cats are.

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:33.250
Uh oh, she's devolved into
a lazy, phone-fiddling magical girl.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.460
<b>TAMA SAKURA</b>

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.460
<b>MANJU BUNS</b>

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.460
<b>Tama</b>

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.460
<b>Zoological</b>

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.460
<b>Park</b>

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:36.330
Here is a little gift as a sign of my good-will.

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:39.830
These are the Tama Sakura Manju Buns
I got from the boss!

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.380
<b>TAMA SAKURA</b>

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.380
<b>MANJU BUNS</b>

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.380
<b>Tama</b>

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.380
<b>Zoological</b>

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.380
<b>Park</b>

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:42.250
I'll eat these and get some glucose
to boost my brain power!

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:43.920
<b>Tama</b>

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:43.920
<b>Zoological</b>

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:43.920
<b>Park</b>

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:43.790
What's this?

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.500
Momo!

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:46.080
What's up?

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:49.500
If you can finish all your homework
before this week is up, then I'll give you these!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.080
Tickets for the zoo?

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:51.750
Yep!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.330
And not just any tickets, these are limited VIP tickets!

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:57.040
I found them in the gifts that I got from my boss.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:59.250
<b>Tama Zoological Park</b>

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:59.130
And there are 7 days left before they expire!

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:11.880
<b>SHLOOOOOOOP</b>

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:02.880
The zoo's probably super packed
this time of year. Hard pass.
Shlooooop. Shlooooop. Shlooooop.<b></b>

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.210
You better quit it with this lazy bumpkin routine.
Shlooooop. Shlooooop. Shlooooop.<b></b>

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:09.330
Also, I think it's pretty sinister to motivate people
by preying on their materialistic desires.
Shlooooop. Shlooooop. Shlooooop.<b></b>

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:11.880
Ugh... You got me there.
Shlooooop. Shlooooop. Shlooooop.<b></b>

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:16.420
But while you're at it, can you tell me
what they have in the VIP section?

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:19.630
Let's see... looks like you get the chance
to play with a baby tiger.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.290
We got 7 days before they expire, right?!

00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:22.540
Ah! She's back at the table!

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:24.750
Let me guess, you're susceptible
to anything that's cat-related!

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:27.290
This is great! She's really gonna do it!

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.880
What a streak of devilishly good luck!

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.540
Hey, Shamiko?

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:31.920
About the essay...

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:38.330
I honestly can't think of anything significant that I want
to do with my future, but in terms of a short-term goal...

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:42.290
I wanna eat a lunch that you spared
no effort to make for me.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:43.750
On a picnic.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.330
Then empty your stomach
because I'll make enough to fill it 3 times over!

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:50.330
I'm gonna finish my homework, too!
Then we can all go together!

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:51.380
A zoo picnic!

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.670
Happy! Happy!

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:56.580
Apparently I was an orphan.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:21:00.380
My sister was kind enough to accompany me
around to various places.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:03.710
I guess Momo's had her own share of hardship.

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:06.630
I know that I can't actually replace Ms. Sakura,

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:07.960
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:09.460
but if I take the time to visit places with Momo,
then maybe someday...

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:07.960
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:07.960
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:09.710
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:09.710
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:09.710
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:11.880
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:11.880
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:11.880
<b>Scratch</b>

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:17.540
You look really weird right now. What are you wearing?!
Did you semi-transform?!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.130
Yeah, it helps boost my focus.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.080
<b>WORLD HISTORY</b>

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.080
<b>VOCABULARY WORKSHEETS</b>

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.080
<b>A FEW DAYS LATER</b>

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:24.920
Shamiko! I got it all done within 3 days! Take a look!

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:29.080
<b>SLUMP...</b>

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.380
Nothing looks like it's changed
since I last saw you. What's going on?

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:31.960
I haven't finished! These math drills are killing me!

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:35.330
I spent this whole time giving it everything
I honestly had, but still couldn't do it!

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:36.670
I'm just not competent enough!

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:39.460
So, in other words, you wasted all your time
in the worst way possible...

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:43.000
I'll never finish my homework at this rate...

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:47.170
I'll make the lunch for you,
so please go to the zoo and enjoy it without me!

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:47.670
Huh?

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:49.040
Don't be silly.

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:51.540
The zoo isn't any fun
unless we're all there together, right?

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.750
You were full of confidence when you said it last time...

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:58.380
"There's nothing more important
than keeping promises" or whatever.

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:01.630
Why did you do a full transformation?! I'm scared!

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:01.630
Tremble, tremble.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:03.080
You're pulling an all-nighter.

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:04.710
We finish your homework at all costs!

00:22:08.710 --> 00:22:10.330
Hey! No sleeping! Wake up!

00:22:11.380 --> 00:22:13.210
Sis... don't give up!

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:15.080
<b>The type who finishes</b>

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:15.080
<b>all of her homework aside</b>

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:15.080
<b>from the diary during July</b>

00:22:15.210 --> 00:22:17.380
Don't think this means... you've won...

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:19.630
Figure out the answers in your sleep!

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:20.830
Don't give up, Shamiko!

00:22:21.130 --> 00:22:25.210
Become a demon smart enough to get
her homework done in a planned and timely manner.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:46.790
Mata aeta ne drama nandatte? (howa howa)

00:22:46.790 --> 00:22:49.790
Sugu (sugu!) oshie ni mo icchauzo (utou!)

00:22:49.960 --> 00:22:52.710
Kakyuuteki naruhaya de (saa!)

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:55.330
Ara post mo "ohayou" nante (pikopiko)

00:22:55.330 --> 00:22:57.540
Mou shippo made saeteru (waa!)

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:01.380
Hakusen o tondette itsu mentsudoeba

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:04.130
Kyou mo hajimatteku

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:07.920
Totsuzen ni mystery

00:23:08.040 --> 00:23:11.290
Kurakura mayou kedo

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:15.830
Te to te o tori doko made susume

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:22.750
Guruguru machi wa mawari kagayaku

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:25.670
Korkoro toehatae shite

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.380
Yume o mazeta yoikagen wa

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:31.330
Kimi ni hana o sakaseru yo

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:34.170
Yomo made kakomu tetragon

00:23:34.290 --> 00:23:37.130
Aa machikado ni hanataba

00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:40.080
Nee ima wa mou sukoshi

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:44.130
Sottosotto sono hana o misete

00:23:44.330 --> 00:23:47.630
Yokubacchaeba mou ikkai

00:23:56.170 --> 00:24:11.080
<b>PREVIEW</b>

00:23:57.210 --> 00:24:01.710
I've decided to ignore the fact I was wearing nothing
but a leaf and only remember the fun parts of the festival!

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:04.630
I hear that you and Momo had a hard time
getting your summer homework done, huh?

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:06.460
Oh yeah? Was it not a problem for you, Mikan?

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:08.460
Well, that's a story I'll share with you another day.

00:24:07.290 --> 00:24:11.080
<b>SPARKS FLY?! LIGHT AND DARK GO ON A JOINT EXCURSION!</b>

00:24:08.460 --> 00:24:09.670
Shamiko, did you make the lunch?

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:10.750
We're going to the zoo!
